{
 "id": "holley",
 "label": "Holley Terminator X / HP / Dominator",
 "manufacturer": "Holley Performance (USA)",
 "models": [
  "Terminator X and X Max (V1-V3)",
  "HP and Dominator (V4 software and later)"
 ],
 "firmware": "Terminator X V1-V3; HP and Dominator V4 or later",
 "bitrate": 1000000,
 "extended": true,
 "timeout_s": 1.0,
 "status": "simulated",
 "source": {
  "title": "Holley EFI 1st Party CAN Communications Protocol, and Holley's published DBC",
  "version": "Revision 1 (8 November 2024); Terminator X V3.dbc",
  "url": "https://www.holley.com/support/fuel_injection/terminator_x_and_x_max/",
  "also": [
   "Terminator X V3.dbc (same IDs as HP & Dominator V6.dbc)"
  ]
 },
 "id_mask": "0x1FFFF800",
 "setup": [
  "The dash's CAN bus must run at 1 Mbit/s (ecu.bitrate 1000000): Holley's CAN is 1 Mbit/s, 29-bit IDs.",
  "The ECU broadcasts all the time; the low 11 bits of each ID are its serial number, so any Holley ECU is read.",
  "Connect to the ECU's CAN wires, with the bus terminated at both ends."
 ],
 "notes": "Holley sends each channel as a float in its own frame, with a status in byte 7 (kept as ecu.holley_status_*; its meaning is not documented). Temperatures come in degrees F, pressures in psi and speed in mph: converted here to C, kPa and km/h. Holley's DBC labels oil and fuel pressure \"PSIa\"; whether they are absolute is not confirmed, so they are converted as sent. Holley's tuning goes through its 558-443 CAN-to-USB interface, whose driver Holley says does not work on ARM.",
 "tuner": {
  "name": "Holley EFI software (Terminator X / HP / Dominator) or Sniper software",
  "runs_on_dash": false,
  "connection": "Holley 558-443 CAN-to-USB interface from a Windows computer (its driver does not work on ARM)",
  "url": "https://www.holley.com/support/fuel_injection/",
  "status": "untested"
 },
